  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "r1-borders",
      "page": "web",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 640,
      "text": "R1 — borders dropped.\nNo HIG separator clears WCAG's 3:1 on any light background (opaqueSeparator measures 1.53–1.71), and this codebase already carried 17 of 24 bordered classes under 3:1. Every boundary here is a fill: sunken → raised → tertiary fill."
    },
    {
      "id": "r2-type",
      "page": "web",
      "x": 700,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 640,
      "text": "R2 — iOS metrics.\nBody 17 / Callout 16 / Subheadline 15 / Footnote 13, clearing the committed 16px body floor. Caption is clamped to 12px rather than HIG's 11 so the label ratchet holds. Controls are 44px; dense in-list rows are 24px, matching the product's own split."
    },
    {
      "id": "palette-note",
      "page": "foundations",
      "x": 1560,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "Apple's STOCK system colors fail 15 of the 27 pairs declared in packages/ui/src/tokens.ts — white on systemBlue is 4.02:1, and Apple does not target WCAG AA for control fills.\n\nThese are Apple's INCREASED-CONTRAST variants, which fail none. success uses the incumbent green700 #1E7A34 rather than Apple's #248A3D, which lands at 4.40 against a 4.5 minimum.\n\nRe-run docs/hig-probe-accessible.py to check any of these numbers."
    }
  ],
  "launch": { "view": "canvas", "page": "web" }
